 R←Test_API_028(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;rc;msg;buff;log;fn1;fn2;h1;h2;folders;folder
⍝ Runs "CompareVersions" on a file that was renamed by a commit. `ChangeLog` follows the file
⍝ across the rename, so it hands out commits that know the file only under its OLD name: asking
⍝ Git for "hash:new" fails.\\
⍝ Works on a private copy of the fixture: the commit would change a history that later test
⍝ cases rely on.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed
 folders←⍬

 tempDir←FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir'APLGit2-',⊃⎕SI
 (##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/CiderProject4.zip')ZipArchive.UnzipTo tempDir
 (rc msg buff)←tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'mv APLSource/Counter.aplf APLSource/Counter2.aplf'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠rc
 (rc msg buff)←tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'commit -m "Counter renamed"'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠rc
 log←tempDir G.ChangeLog'APLSource/Counter2.aplf'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 4≠≢log                          ⍝ The rename plus the three commits before it

 ⍝ No hashes: the rename commit, and the commit before it, which knows only "Counter.aplf"
 (fn1 fn2 h1 h2)←tempDir G.CompareVersions'APLSource/Counter2.aplf'
 folders,←⊂⊃⎕NPARTS fn1
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/' r←3'⍷⊃⎕NGET fn1
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/' r←3'⍷⊃⎕NGET fn2

 ⍝ An older commit that changed the file ("Counter bumped to 2"), compared with the rename commit
 (fn1 fn2 h1 h2)←tempDir G.CompareVersions'APLSource/Counter2.aplf'((⊂3 1)⊃log)
 folders,←⊂⊃⎕NPARTS fn1
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/' r←2'⍷⊃⎕NGET fn1
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/' r←3'⍷⊃⎕NGET fn2

 ⍝ A commit that did NOT change the file ("README extended"): its path must be inferred
 (fn1 fn2 h1 h2)←tempDir G.CompareVersions'APLSource/Counter2.aplf'((⊂1 1)⊃tempDir G.ChangeLog'README.md')
 folders,←⊂⊃⎕NPARTS fn1
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/' r←3'⍷⊃⎕NGET fn1

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 :For folder :In folders
     {}FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce folder
 :EndFor
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
